Perfect 👍
What you want is a format-selection download popup like:

> “Do you want to download as: PDF / Excel / Image?”



Below is a clean, working, engineering-project ready solution (no confusion).


---

✅ FINAL SOLUTION: FORMAT SELECTION DOWNLOAD

🎯 Flow

1. User clicks Download Health Summary


2. Popup appears → PDF | Excel | Image


3. Selected format downloads




---

🖥️ STEP 1: Download Button

<button onclick="openDownloadOptions()">
  Download Health Summary
</button>


---

🪟 STEP 2: Format Selection Popup (Modal)

<div id="downloadModal" style="display:none; position:fixed; top:30%; left:50%; transform:translate(-50%, -50%);
background:white; padding:20px; box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.3); z-index:1000;">

  <h3>Select Download Format</h3>

  <button onclick="downloadPDF()">📄 PDF</button>
  <button onclick="downloadExcel()">📊 Excel</button>
  <button onclick="downloadImage()">🖼 Image</button>
  <br><br>
  <button onclick="closeDownloadOptions()">Cancel</button>
</div>


---

⚙️ STEP 3: JavaScript Logic

<script>
function openDownloadOptions() {
  document.getElementById("downloadModal").style.display = "block";
}

function closeDownloadOptions() {
  document.getElementById("downloadModal").style.display = "none";
}

// PDF (Simple Browser Print)
function downloadPDF() {
  closeDownloadOptions();
  window.print();
}

// Excel (CSV format)
function downloadExcel() {
  closeDownloadOptions();

  const data = `Field,Value
Name,Vishnu
Attendance,92%
Stress Level,Low
Screen Time,Moderate`;

  const blob = new Blob([data], { type: "text/csv" });
  const link = document.createElement("a");
  link.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  link.download = "Health_Summary.xlsx";
  link.click();
}

// Image (PNG)
function downloadImage() {
  closeDownloadOptions();
  alert("Image download requires canvas/html2canvas");
}
</script>


---

🖼️ STEP 4: Image Download (IMPORTANT)

Add html2canvas library:

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/html2canvas@1.4.1/dist/html2canvas.min.js"></script>

Then use:

function downloadImage() {
  closeDownloadOptions();

  html2canvas(document.getElementById("healthSummary")).then(canvas => {
    const link = document.createElement("a");
    link.download = "Health_Summary.png";
    link.href = canvas.toDataURL();
    link.click();
  });
}


---

📌 SUPPORTED FORMATS

Format	Use

PDF	Official report
Excel	Data analysis
Image	Sharing



---

🔐 ROLE-BASED ACCESS

Student: Own health summary only

Admin: Any student / class



---

🎓 PROJECT PRESENTATION LINE

> “EduMitra AI provides multi-format downloads allowing users and administrators to export health summaries as PDF, Excel, or Image based on their needs.”




---

🚀 NEXT UPGRADES

PDF with logo & signature

Admin bulk download

Email report automatically

Language-based reports


