Ah! I understand exactly what’s happening 😅 — the “Locate Me” or current position syncing is not working. Usually in Leaflet + React, this happens because of a few common issues:


---

🔎 WHY SYNCING CURRENT POSITION FAILS

1. Map reference not initialized

mapRef.current might be null when navigator.geolocation tries to call setView.



2. Marker placement logic

If markerPosition state is not updated properly, dragging or location update won’t reflect.



3. Geolocation async issue

navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition is async. If map isn’t ready yet, the position is lost.



4. React re-render resets map

If you recreate the map on every render, the marker disappears.



5. Zoom level / map bounds not updated

map.setView([lat, lng], zoom) must be called after map is fully initialized.





---

✅ FIX: SYNC CURRENT POSITION CORRECTLY

Here’s a robust way to do it in React + Leaflet:

const locateMe = () => {
  if (!navigator.geolocation) {
    alert("Geolocation not supported by your browser.");
    return;
  }

  navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
    (position) => {
      const { latitude, longitude } = position.coords;

      // Make sure map is initialized
      if (!mapRef.current) return;

      const map = mapRef.current;

      // Center map to current location
      map.setView([latitude, longitude], 15);

      // Place marker at current location
      placeMarker([latitude, longitude]);
